  "description": "Typed, checked LLM calls for .NET and C#. The core package: send a value and an intent to a model and get your own type back, checked in your process against your type and your rules, with a retry on the findings, within the limits you set. IntentSharp lets developers express application behavior as intent, apply it to ordinary .NET values and methods, and connect it to any technology, such as a database or an API, through ITarget, which the developer implements. Models come from an external provider file: the core ships the openai and anthropic kinds, and a developer can add a kind of their own. Policy lives in versioned documents that reload while the application runs: intent files with IntentSharp.Catalog and rule files with IntentSharp.Guardrails. The core provides versioned document stores with revert, and it detects a changed target, document or provider file and runs your change handlers before the next target operation continues. Our estimate for a typical business application is 20 to 40% less application code. Every project needs this package, and a project whose calls are inline or [AIIntent] methods needs only this one. Add IntentSharp.Catalog to keep intents in YAML or JSON files, IntentSharp.Guardrails to keep rule sets in files, and IntentSharp.Extensions.AI to run on any Microsoft.Extensions.AI IChatClient, such as Ollama or Azure OpenAI, or to give catalog intents to agents as AIFunction tools. It provides strongly typed LLM responses on values, collections and [AIIntent] methods; structured output checked in your process against your type and your rules on every answer, cached or fresh; caps on attempts, model calls, output tokens and time; a result that reports success, the value, every issue and every attempt; a request cache and rate limiting; and AddIntentSharp for dependency injection. Commercial software, not open source: evaluate free for 30 days on development and test systems; after that, business use needs a paid license, and production use needs one from the first day (intentsharp.com/pricing).",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
